      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add transactional rollback for managed updates",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nManaged npm updates previously replaced the live package before the replacement Gateway was proven healthy. Package-only rollback was unsafe because the restarted process could commit existing Doctor/package migrations before confirmation.\n\nThis draft implements the refined transaction boundary: verify the newly installed package without mutating state, snapshot state before activation, restart normally, wait for health plus initiating-channel confirmation, then either clean up or restore package and state in strict order.\n\n## Design Deltas\n\n- Adds `openclaw gateway verify`: loads config, opens shared and agent SQLite stores read-only without migrations, initializes provider/model discovery far enough to prove the binary and dependencies, prints a machine-readable result, and exits.\n- Runs that probe through the managed Node and newly staged package root before service restart. Probe failure restores retention immediately; no restart or state mutation occurs.\n- Snapshots the state directory before activation. Darwin tries APFS clone copy, Linux tries required reflinks, then falls back to per-database `VACUUM INTO` plus a complete non-database state/config copy. External and symlinked config targets are preserved. Managed install subtrees nested under state are excluded from state rollback while the rollback image itself remains retryable.\n- Reworks `update-handover.ts` to the honest sequence: `verify -> snapshot -> swap -> restart -> healthy -> confirm -> complete`, with `rolling-back -> rolled-back / failed` compensation.\n- Extends the detached managed-update helper into the transaction owner. Rollback order is enforced as service stop, retained package restore, state snapshot restore, retained service start.\n- Persists the transaction marker in the existing restart-sentinel SQLite surface and a recovery journal beside the snapshot. No SQLite schema-version or Gateway protocol-version bump.\n- Records initiating session/channel/to/account/thread plus delivery or human confirmation tier. The replacement Gateway sends the post-update notice; delivery acknowledgement auto-confirms delivery tier, while human tier requires the matching challenge reply.\n- Gates all normal inbound work during rollback-capable probation. Dispatch-capable callbacks are dual-written to candidate and retained queues before confirmation; observe-only callbacks fail confirmation and force rollback because the retained package cannot safely replay their admission shape.\n- Adds stable notice idempotency by handoff ID, durable replay-admission fences, owner leases, interrupted-update recovery, confirmed-cleanup retry, and fail-closed recovery when terminal journal/status persistence or retained-service activation fails.\n- Keeps Round 1 install-class gating: only verified managed local-prefix npm layouts receive transactional rollback. Unmanaged npm globals warn and point to the website managed installer; other install classes keep existing behavior.\n- Adds status, Doctor, changelog, CLI, and restart-recovery narration for pending, confirmed-cleanup, rolled-back, and failed transactions.\n\n## Main Surfaces\n\n- Verify primitive: `src/gateway/startup-verify.ts`, `src/cli/gateway-cli/register-verify.ts`\n- Snapshot/restore: `src/infra/update-state-snapshot.ts`\n- State machine: `src/infra/update-handover.ts`\n- Durable marker/journal: `src/infra/update-transaction-marker.ts`, `src/infra/update-recovery-journal.ts`\n- Detached orchestration/recovery: `src/cli/update-cli/update-command-post-update.ts`, `src/infra/update-managed-service-handoff.ts`, `src/infra/update-interrupted-recovery.ts`\n- Gateway confirmation/probation: `src/infra/update-confirmation-runtime.ts`, `src/gateway/server-restart-sentinel.ts`\n- Operator narration: `src/commands/status-update-restart.ts`, `src/commands/doctor-gateway-daemon-flow.ts`, `docs/cli/update.md`, `docs/gateway/restart-recovery.md`\n\n## Install-Class Coverage\n\n| Install class | Behavior in this draft |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verified managed local-prefix npm install with owned service | Full verify, snapshot, restart, confirmation, cleanup, and package+state rollback |\n| Unmanaged npm global | Detect and warn; point to managed website installer; no transactional mutation |\n| pnpm/Bun global, Git checkout, unowned/lookalike layout | Existing update path; no managed rollback claim |\n\n`OPENCLAW_UPDATE_NO_ROLLBACK=1` remains the explicit bypass. No new config or environment surface was added.\n\n## Isolated End-to-End Simulation Transcripts\n\nAll three run with fake package roots, fake state, and stub Gateway/service steps under temporary directories.\n\nSuccessful verify plus delivery confirmation:\n\n```text\nverify:ok\nsnapshot:state\nswap:package\nservice:restart\nhealth:ok\nconfirm:acked\ncleanup:snapshot\n```\n\nVerify failure; retained package restored without restart:\n\n```text\nverify:failed\nfailed:new package startup verification failed\nrollback:package\n```\n\nHealthy replacement without confirmation; full rollback:\n\n```text\nverify:ok\nsnapshot:state\nswap:package\nservice:restart\nhealth:ok\nconfirm:timeout\nfailed:delivery confirmation timed out\nrollback:stop\nrollback:package\nrollback:state\nrollback:start\n```\n\n## Validation\n\nFinal-head Blacksmith Testbox proof:\n\n- `pnpm tsgo:core`\n- `pnpm tsgo:core:test`\n- `pnpm build`\n- Exact touched test set: 27 files, 429 tests, 6 Vitest shards, all green\n- `git diff --check`\n- Fresh autoreview after all fixes: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n\nHeavy proof run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29671737434\n\nAn earlier broad `pnpm test:changed` fan-out also reached unrelated UI/Vault/QA baseline failures, and `pnpm check:changed` reached existing max-lines ratchets in state/UI files. The final exact touched proof and full build are green.\n\n## Safety Boundary and Remaining Gaps\n\n- Draft only. No real state directory, Gateway service, LaunchAgent, systemd unit, or Windows task was touched. All mutation/recovery proof is isolated or stubbed.\n- No live OS-service-manager crash injection yet. The generated helper is exercised as a child process with filesystem and command faults, but not against a real launchd/systemd installation under this work order.\n- Replay intentionally preserves the shipped text, route, provenance, reply, thread, and compact media-note shape. It does not invent a compatibility queue for richer future callbacks; observe-only admission triggers rollback instead.\n- Transactional coverage remains intentionally limited to the verified managed local-prefix npm layout. Broad global-package and Git rollback remain out of scope.\n- Retained package stays after a confirmed update for the next update/recovery point. The state snapshot and transaction marker are removed only after durable confirmation/probation release; cleanup is lease-guarded and retryable.\n- Catastrophic simultaneous loss of both detached processes relies on next-Gateway startup recovery from the durable marker/journal. Real-machine proof remains intentionally absent here.\n\nThis supersedes the prior documented blocker. Doctor/package migration ordering remains unchanged: the pre-restart verify mode performs no migration, while normal migrations happen only after the snapshot exists and are reversed by full state restore on rollback.\n",
